{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0298"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/countries","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__countries.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",176],["+","country as a whole holds two water records. Canada has the longest coastline of any country in the world, about 243,000 kilometres according to Statistics Canada, along three oceans and the countless islands of the Arctic archipelago. And its ice-scoured Shield is so full of water that Canada contains more than half of all the world's natural lakes – about 62 per cent of the lakes larger than ten hectares, according to a 2016 global survey.\n\nThe "],["=",991]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",158],["+","Das Land als Ganzes hält zwei Wasserrekorde. Kanada hat die längste Küste aller Länder der Welt, nach Statistics Canada rund 243.000 Kilometer, an drei Ozeanen und um die unzähligen Inseln des arktischen Archipels. Und sein von Gletschern abgeschliffener Kanadischer Schild ist so wasserreich, dass in Kanada mehr als die Hälfte aller natürlichen Seen der Welt liegt – rund 62 Prozent der Seen über zehn Hektar, wie eine weltweite Erhebung von 2016 ergab.\n\n"],["=",927]]}]},
